COST TOO MUCH TO PUMP OUT.

172
00:09:05,588 --> 00:09:07,547
BUT WITH THE PRICE
OF OIL SKY-HIGH,

173
00:09:07,547 --> 00:09:09,984
OIL SANDS ARE WORTH WORKIN'.

174
00:09:09,984 --> 00:09:15,337
WE'RE TALKING $50 MILLION,
$60 MILLION TO THE LANDOWNERS.

175
00:09:15,337 --> 00:09:17,295
SO YOU TOOK THE GERBERS
TO COURT.

176
00:09:17,295 --> 00:09:19,689
YEAH...

177
00:09:19,689 --> 00:09:21,212
LAST YEAR.

178
00:09:21,212 --> 00:09:23,475
AND WHAT
DO YOU THINK HAPPENED?

179
00:09:23,475 --> 00:09:25,216
YOU GOT NOTHING.

180
00:09:25,216 --> 00:09:27,262
ZERO.

181
00:09:27,262 --> 00:09:29,699
I KNEW I SHOULDN'T
HAVE WASTED MY TIME,

182
00:09:29,699 --> 00:09:33,094
BUT THE DECEIT AND DISHONESTY
HAS MADE ME MAD.

183
00:09:33,094 --> 00:09:35,270
WHERE WERE YOU YESTERDAY,
TED?

184
00:09:35,270 --> 00:09:39,753
WELL, I WAS SEVERAL PLACES,
KIMBALL.

185
00:09:39,753 --> 00:09:41,755
WE'RE GONNA NEED A LIST.

186
00:09:41,755 --> 00:09:44,148
"WE"? I ONLY SEE ONE OF YOU.

187
00:09:44,148 --> 00:09:47,108
I AND THE STATE MACHINERY
OPPRESSION'S

188
00:09:47,108 --> 00:09:49,110
GONNA NEED A LIST.

189
00:09:49,110 --> 00:09:52,113
WELL, I WILL THINK IT OVER.

190
00:09:52,113 --> 00:09:55,072
SOME PEOPLE JUST DON'T
HAVE THAT FACILITY.

191
00:09:55,072 --> 00:09:57,422
I'M SURE YOUR FATHER
LOVED YOU IN HIS WAY.

192
00:09:57,422 --> 00:10:02,210
HE JUST DIDN'T HAVE THE TOOLS
TO EXPRESS THAT LOVE.

193
00:10:02,210 --> 00:10:04,212
[voice breaking]
YOU KNOW WHAT, MAN?

194
00:10:04,212 --> 00:10:06,823
I REALLY APPRECIATE YOU
LISTENING TO ME, MAN.

195
00:10:06,823 --> 00:10:10,174
PLEASE, BOO.
WHAT ARE CELLMATES FOR?

196
00:10:26,147 --> 00:10:28,149
[exhales]

197
00:10:28,149 --> 00:10:29,454
SO LISTEN.

198
00:10:29,454 --> 00:10:31,195
LISTENING.

199
00:10:31,195 --> 00:10:34,068
ABOUT THE, UH,

200
00:10:34,068 --> 00:10:37,288
UNFORTUNATE SITUATION
WITH JANE,

201
00:10:37,288 --> 00:10:40,248
I WANT YOU TO KNOW

202
00:10:40,248 --> 00:10:42,816
THAT MY BEEF
IS ONLY WITH HIM.

203
00:10:42,816 --> 00:10:45,296
I GOT NO PROBLEM
WITH YOU OR YOUR PEOPLE.

204
00:10:47,342 --> 00:10:51,085
IT WAS A BIG MISTAKE BRINGING IN
A WHACK JOB LIKE HIM,

205
00:10:51,085 --> 00:10:54,001
BUT THAT'S IN THE PAST NOW.

206
00:10:55,785 --> 00:10:58,396
YOU AND ME...

207
00:10:58,396 --> 00:11:01,791
YOU AND ME ALWAYS HAD
A GOOD WORKING RELATIONSHIP,

208
00:11:01,791 --> 00:11:03,967
AND I HOPE THAT CAN CONTINUE.

209
00:11:03,967 --> 00:11:06,187
OKAY.

210
00:11:06,187 --> 00:11:07,579
I LISTENED.

211
00:11:07,579 --> 00:11:10,582
SO WE'RE COOL?

212
00:11:10,582 --> 00:11:13,977
YOU DID WHAT YOU THOUGHT
WAS RIGHT.

213
00:11:13,977 --> 00:11:18,068
I NEED TO THINK ABOUT IT BEFORE
I KNOW WHETHER WE'RE COOL.

214
00:11:18,068 --> 00:11:21,071
OKAY.

215
00:11:21,071 --> 00:11:23,030
OKAY, FAIR ENOUGH.

216
00:11:29,950 --> 00:11:31,995
[Patrick yawns]

217
00:11:31,995 --> 00:11:33,867
GOOD NIGHT, JANE.

218
00:11:36,347 --> 00:11:38,698
GOOD NIGHT, PAL.

219
00:11:38,698 --> 00:11:41,135
AND DON'T WORRY
ABOUT TOMORROW MORNING.

220
00:11:43,224 --> 00:11:45,835
WHY WOULD I NEED TO WORRY
ABOUT TOMORROW MORNING?

221
00:11:45,835 --> 00:11:47,837
THERE ARE SOME
SCARY PEOPLE HERE.

222
00:11:47,837 --> 00:11:49,926
THEY ALL KNOW YOU'RE A COP.

223
00:11:49,926 --> 00:11:54,452
HOW WOULD THEY KNOW THAT?
